{"changes":["eka-core v1.11.0: new leaf package pathglob (Compile/Interpret/Match) implementing the Standard 1.5 grammar — `*` within a segment, `?` one character, `**` across segments (zero-segment included), whole-path anchored; `**` must be a whole segment, empty pattern refused. New contexts.(*Engine).UnitsForPath(projectID, sourceRepo, path) returns the matching units of ONE repository (repo-scoped, not project-scoped: patterns are repo-root-relative). Malformed `appliesTo` (non-string element or uninterpretable pattern) is a structural (R0) blocking violation in conformance, wired into Validate and ValidateCKO; absence is not a violation.","eka-cli v1.23.0: `eka context --for \u003cpath\u003e` mode. The subject (identity) and --for modes are mutually exclusive; --for emits the `eka-constraints-v1` object ({schema,path,constraints:[Entry]}) with the existing --json/--compact contract, or a human projection; an empty set prints and exits 0. Paths normalize to repository-root-relative (relative resolved against the cwd then the repo root, so it works from a subdirectory; absolute relativized; escaping the repo refused). Depends on eka-core v1.11.0."],"role":"implementation","summary":"M1 runtime half: the `eka context --for \u003cpath\u003e` path-to-constraint retrieval is implemented and released across eka-core and eka-cli. A repository-relative path now returns exactly the units whose declared `appliesTo` scope matches it — deterministically ordered (authority stratum ascending, then canonical identity), one hop, no similarity search; a path matching nothing yields an empty set, not an error. Remaining M1 acceptance criteria — the repo-level \"a well-formed pattern matches no path\" warning and the noise measurement — are NOT yet done, so this work item stays in-progress.","tests":["eka-core: go test -race -cover ./... — all packages green (coverage gate: added the pathglob floor, 90). pathglob glob-grammar table + malformed; conformance malformed→R0 and absent/valid→clean; contexts ordering (stratum then identity), empty set, repository scoping, malformed→error, absent-binds-nothing.","eka-cli: anvil pipeline ci success — format, vet, windows cross-compile, eka verify (PASS), unit-tests (cmd 632s); PR CI green incl. the linux/windows installer e2e. cmd/context_for_test.go covers matching, empty set, --json schema, subject+--for conflict, absolute/relative/outside paths, and the subdirectory resolution case."]}